     The order doesn't matter.  The restriction is that you
can only use letters that have already been assigned to spells.
So if you happen to know 4 spells, then the only available
letter choices are a, b, c, and d.  To assign one to 'e', you'd
need to know at least 5 spells.  And to move something away
from 'y', you'd have to put something else into that letter,
since the letter control works by exchanging pairs of spells.

     No one has mentioned the paranoid confirmation patch yet.
